A||||3||Muscleboy||Speaker Covers
Z||000000||Muscleboy||08-10-99||01:18 PM||||I just replaced all the speakers in my '87 Pont GT.  The front speaker covers in the dash popped right off.  However, the speaker covers in the back panel weren't that easy.  I ended up breaking all the pegs that keep it in the back panel.  Should I have actually removed the panel???  I can order a new left cover from the dealer but not a right one.<p>Any ideas??  Also...if you in Maryland close to Baltimore or Frederick let me know....
Z||000001||Bruce||08-10-99||06:19 PM||||What kind of speakers did you install?
Z||000002||BluByYou||08-11-99||12:07 PM||||Well, the answer is "yes" - to removing the whole panel.  I put Boston Acoustic's in when I changed my rear speakers - didn't remove the whole panel, just loosened it at the top and flexed it inward (towards the interior) enough to get the job done.  The reason?  Because I broke ONE peg and said "no more".  Anyway, I glued the corner of the cover that I broke.  Many adhesives will do the job, but consider the two parts - you'll need something fairly viscous (Elmer's won't do). 
Z||000003||batboy||08-11-99||07:33 PM||||I kind of broke one of the rear speaker grills too before I realized that you are supposed to remove the whole trim panel. I used some "Shoe Goo" and glued the grill back on. I haven't had any problems since then.
